  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive Reintegration for Improving the Quality of Life of Communities within the Framework of the Plans with a Territorial Approach (PDET) Roadmap in Colombia and Conpes 3931</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the aim of further contributing to the peacebuilding and stabilization process in Colombia, it is necessary to strengthen and implement a comprehensive reincorporation process that in turn improves the quality of life of the communities within the framework of the Plans with a Territorial Approach (PDET in Spanish) roadmap. This is in accordance with the provisions of the National Policy for Social and Economic Reincorporation of Former Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia&#x2014;People&apos;s Army (FARC-EP in Spanish) Members (i.e. Conpes 3931 of 2018), and section 5.6 of the Stabilization Policy &#x201c;Peace with Legality&#x201d;. Given this context, IOM and the Agency for Reincorporation and Normalization have signed an agreement with the objective of joining technical, administrative and financial efforts aimed at contributing to the implementation of the National Policy for the Social and Economic Reincorporation of Former FARC-EP Members, through actions directed towards the comprehensive reincorporation and improvement of the quality of life of the communities within the framework of the PDET roadmap and Conpes 3931 of 2018. The expected outcomes of the lines of action are technical assistance to national and territorial institutions and support to improve the quality of life and strengthen community organizational processes.</narrative>
  </description>
